From: NimbleZero <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] panel-mipi-dbi-m: put the panel to sleep when the display is switched off

When the display pipe is disabled (FBIOBLANK powerdown, DPMS off) the controller kept
scanning with only the backlight off.  Send DISPLAY_OFF and ENTER_SLEEP_MODE first; the
enable path already resets the panel and re-runs the init commands, which leave sleep.

Measured on a Cardputer Zero 2026-11-23 (battery, backlight off, Wi-Fi on): 209 -> 202 mA,
TE pulses 62/s -> 0.

--- a/modules/st7789v-1.0/panel-mipi-dbi-m.c	2026-11-23 13:48:42.284629875 -0500
+++ b/modules/st7789v-1.0/panel-mipi-dbi-m.c	2026-11-23 13:49:47.870289485 -0500
@@ -877,6 +877,11 @@
 
     flush_work(&panel->nz_work);
     mutex_lock(&panel->display_lock);
+    /* Put the controller to sleep: it stops scanning and its TE output goes quiet
+     * (hardware 2026-11-23: -6 to -7 mA with the backlight already off, TE 62/s -> 0).
+     * The enable path resets and re-runs the init commands, which leave sleep mode. */
+    mipi_dbi_command(&dbidev->dbi, MIPI_DCS_SET_DISPLAY_OFF);
+    mipi_dbi_command(&dbidev->dbi, MIPI_DCS_ENTER_SLEEP_MODE);
     mipi_dbi_pipe_disable(pipe);
     mutex_unlock(&panel->display_lock);
 }
